litterbox-qt (0.1-53) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebase rejected stale card orders against a fresh server snapshot with a
    new operation identity. Retire explicitly not-found operations durably,
    separately from acknowledgements, without erasing original draft bytes.
  * Retry and Sync mail now request a fresh snapshot even while offline,
    without changing automatic refresh gating.
  * Expose the offline Retry action to accessibility with a 48dp minimum target.
  * Reader painted Back/Archive bar buttons directly tappable, with compact
    single-row phone header, slim app bar under 64px and 48dp targets (R59).
  * Complete offline mail prefetch: download and persist every card body during
    synchronization, bounded to two outstanding requests, with durable content-
    sync completion tracking across restart and reconnect (R9).
  * Left-aligned navigation drawer with distinct destination icons, visible
    selected state, scrim/Back dismissal without list anchor loss (R55).
  * Finite operation-error overlays dismiss after approximately eight seconds;
    repeated background retries do not recreate the toast. Durable pending/Retry
    and local-storage errors remain actionable (R55).
  * Unambiguous "Sync mail" and "Check for app updates" command labels in
    English, Russian and Belarusian translations, with equivalent explicit
    wording (R39).
  * Bounded wrapped scrolling overflow menu: inbox commands and reader actions
    fit the usable phone viewport at default and 150% text scale, with labels
    wrapping rather than clipping, reachable through a scrollable ListView (R60,
    R70).
  * Offline status now tracks durable body persistence separately from
    connectivity: contentSyncIncomplete and mailSyncComplete report whether
    every open mail has a persisted original (R9).
  * API body GET requests use a 60-second transfer timeout; stalled transfers
    release their slot for retry without overlapping the old HTTP request.
  * Prefetch queue handles HTTP 429 with a shared one-minute cooldown and
    per-card exponential backoff (up to 60 s), preserving retry across
    reconnects (R59).
  * Reader opens a cached body immediately without a network request when
    available offline; missing bodies request only when online (R9).
  * Navigation drawer uses left-aligned labels in a common icon column with
    compact content-sized spacing, no separate Close destination (R55).
  * Mobileux test coverage: error expiry without acknowledging pending writes,
    sync time requires durable content not connectivity, auth and local-storage
    errors remain actionable after error expiry, overflow dismissal preserves
    list anchor (R55,R59,R60,R70).
  * Keep crash uploads isolated from mail request limits and retain reports
    after interrupted acknowledgements; serialize persistence with revocation.
  * Fix drawer font loading and validate Android imports against packaged
    production resources.
  * Mail manual dragging is disabled while non-mail cards remain reorderable
    (no-mail-reorder).
  * Automatic private Android crash reports are retained locally until a
    matching durable acknowledgement; uploads use the existing per-device
    token-authenticated diagnostics endpoint (automatic private crash
    diagnostics).
